From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:27:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] Restart controls in Settings > About

Settings > About gets a Restart group:
- Reload window reloads only the renderer; backends and turns go on.
- Restart T3 Code stops every backend the normal way and relaunches.
- Hard restart gives backends 3 s, then kills each one's process tree
  (taskkill /T /F on Windows, SIGKILL elsewhere) and, for a WSL backend
  on a staged runtime, every process in the distro running from that
  exact runtime directory with its descendants (wsl.exe -e sh -c with
  the directory as a positional argument, 5 s timeout, best effort),
  then relaunches.
Both restarts ask first. A plain browser shows only Reload window.

On Windows, when T3CODE_CUSTOMIZE_RELAUNCH names an existing launch.ps1,
a relaunch starts that launcher (hidden, -WaitPid <main pid>) and quits
instead of calling app.relaunch, so a rebuilt build opens next time.
